[([tabosc4~] is a traditional computer music style wavetable lookup oscillator)]
[(using 4-point polynomial interpolation. The table should have a power of two)]
[(points plus three "guard points", one at the beginning and two at the end,)]
[(which should be wraparound copies of the last point and the first two points,)]
[(respectively. The "sinesum" and "cosinesum" methods for arrays do this)]
[(automatically for you if you just want to specify partial strengths.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
